                        "rating":  4,
                        "text":  {
                                     "text":  "Before we take a walk to Lungshan temple, we tried the local foods around. Takes about 3 minute walk from the station.\n\nWe tried some of their foods:\n• Stew minced pork : it was a good combination to mix warm rice and fats from minced pork, taste more to sweet, pour it with wonton soup made it slurpy was best.\n• Stew pork belly : portion big and price was friendly to pocket, texture was incredibly tender, despite the whole plate mostly fats, but still worth it.\n• Wonton soup : broth was fresh and light, solid filling with pork meats.\n\nThey have outdoor \u0026 indoor seats, quick serving time, but the staff was too cold.",
                                     "languageCode":  "en"
                                 },
